==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*memzrom}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*mḗms|*mḗms, *mēms-rom|flesh}}. Probably the suffix comes from {{affix|la|-brum|t1=instrumental suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|membrum}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|membrum|membrī|n|second}}

# {{lb|la|anatomy}} [[limb]] of the body; [[member]].
# {{lb|la|euphemistic}} the [[penis]] ([[membrum virile|membrum virīle]])
# a [[portion]], [[division]]
# [[apartment]], [[room]] in a house
# member of the [[state]]
# {{lb|la|Late Latin|Christianity}} member of the [[Body of Christ]], member of the [[church]]
# {{lb|la|grammar}} [[clause]] of a sentence

